WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.480
The database address is baked into your image.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.165
So you build one image for dev, one for staging, and one for production.

3
00:00:08.185 --> 00:00:13.140
This port has three tools: ConfigMaps, Secrets, and Kustomize.

4
00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:15.850
First: take the config out of the image.

5
00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.425
A ConfigMap holds keys and values.

6
00:00:18.445 --> 00:00:21.510
The pod gets them as variables or as files.

7
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.823
A change does not restart your pods.

8
00:00:23.843 --> 00:00:27.460
Variables keep the old value until a restart.

9
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.645
Second: passwords and keys.

10
00:00:29.665 --> 00:00:31.095
A Secret looks hidden.

11
00:00:31.115 --> 00:00:33.333
But base64 is an encoding.

12
00:00:33.353 --> 00:00:35.180
Anyone can decode it.

13
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.755
The real protection is access rules, and encryption of the store.

14
00:00:39.775 --> 00:00:42.440
Third: one base, many environments.

15
00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:43.753
You keep one base.

16
00:00:43.773 --> 00:00:46.750
Each environment adds a small patch on top.

17
00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:50.063
A generated ConfigMap gets a new name when it changes.

18
00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.325
So the pods roll.

19
00:00:52.345 --> 00:00:54.310
Quick recap of config.

20
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.922
One image everywhere.

21
00:00:55.942 --> 00:00:58.135
base64 is not encryption.

22
00:00:58.155 --> 00:01:00.745
And a config change needs a rollout.

23
00:01:00.765 --> 00:01:03.865
Now start the first lesson below.
